    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/?source=google.com": {
      "title": "World-changing ideas begin with world-changing people",
      "description": "Homepage · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Start your search today World-changing ideas begin with world-changing people Join #TeamUofG At the University of Glasgow, we are committed to fostering an inspiring and collaborative environment that drives education, research, and innovation. As one of the world’s leading universities, we are always looking for talented and ambitious individuals to join our vibrant community. We are a place that inspires ambitious people to succeed. A place where inquiring minds can develop their ideas. A place where talented people are given the space to realise their dreams. Most importantly, we are open to the world. Our doors are always open, regardless of background. To continue to be a world-class and progressive univer sity, we are dedicated to bringing inspiring people together to change the world.‌ Please read on to discover what it's like to work with us, and the benefits that we offer our colleagues. ​ Please see our Applicant Guide for guidance on creating an account, writing a cover letter, and navigating our website. Thank you for visiting our new Jobs at UofG website. Please be advised that if you held an account on our previous vacancy platform, you will need to create a new account by clicking the 'Register' option at the top right of your screen. If you held an account on our previous vacancy platform, we recommend that you register with the same email address. Culture & values Culture & values We identified values in consultation and partnership with our staff and students. Living and upholding these values will ensure that we remain true to the spirit of our community and ourselves. Benefits, salary and flexible working Benefits, salary and flexible working As one of the world’s leading universities, we are committed to creating an environment where our colleagues feel valued and supported. Your talent and contributions are essential to our global aspirations, and that’s why we invest in you. We offer a competitive and comprehensive package of employee benefits to recognise the value you bring to our team. Relocating to Glasgow Relocating to Glasgow Information about accommodation, life in Glasgow, money advice, relocation, expenses and healthcare Our Strategy: World Changing Glasgow - University for the World Our Strategy: World Changing Glasgow - University for the World Our strategy sets out a bold ambition to transform lives through ideas and action grounded in world leading research, teaching and innovation. This is a strategy rooted in ambition and grounded in reality. We are among the world’s leading universities, but we aspire to be the best university for the world. At it’s heart our strategy is about partnership, with our students, our colleagues, our city and our global community of alumni and partners. Together we will shape a future that reflects our values, builds on our strengths, and recognises our shared responsibility to make a positive difference Real Voices. Real Experiences Ann Hastings HR Operations Manager I have worked at the University of Glasgow all of my adult life and still love working in such a diverse environment with super bright people. Looking back, my highlights are all the jobs I have done although moving to People and Organisational Development was a revelation (in a good way!!). I love the University of Glasgow and could not imagine having worked anywhere else. Ali Salik Organic Geochemistry Technician/Technician Commitment Co-Ordinator ​My professional journey has progressed from modern apprentice in 2012, through technician and senior analytical technician to lab manager.  And in 2021 I was appointed as the University's Technician Commitment Coordinator. Currently, I balance both roles, contributing to the University's commitment to technical excellence. ​I contributed to cutting-edge environmental research initiatives facing the challenges of climate change. Alison Wallace Deputy Director of College Professional Services, College of MVLS I started in 2000 with a temporary role, before being promoted to departmental manager, Head of Academic and Student  Administration and my current post in September 2023. ​My career highlight is the fantastic colleagues I have had over the years who have made the work and the University a great place to be. Craig Daly Professor of Physiology, School of Cardiovasular & Metabolic Health I began as  a Trainee Technician at the University of Glasgow in July 1980, progressing  through the technical career ladder, reaching Grade 6 by the early 1990s due to  my experience working in a research lab.In 1994, I  transitioned from technical to academic roles, becoming a Research Associate  while completing a part-time PhD. After earning my PhD, I advanced to Research  Fellow, achieving Grade 8 on today’s scale, and latterly was ultimately  promoted to senior lecturer and professor. I served on the University  Court (2019-23) as a Union Rep . Having started as a trainee technician, to then be a trustee of the organisation was something that my 17-year-old self could never have imagined. Ann Hastings HR Operations Manager I have worked at the University of Glasgow all of my adult life and still love working in such a diverse environment with super bright people. Looking back, my highlights are all the jobs I have done although moving to People and Organisational Development was a revelation (in a good way!!). I love the University of Glasgow and could not imagine having worked anywhere else. Ali Salik Organic Geochemistry Technician/Technician Commitment Co-Ordinator ​My professional journey has progressed from modern apprentice in 2012, through technician and senior analytical technician to lab manager.  And in 2021 I was appointed as the University's Technician Commitment Coordinator. Currently, I balance both roles, contributing to the University's commitment to technical excellence. ​I contributed to cutting-edge environmental research initiatives facing the challenges of climate change. Alison Wallace Deputy Director of College Professional Services, College of MVLS I started in 2000 with a temporary role, before being promoted to departmental manager, Head of Academic and Student  Administration and my current post in September 2023. ​My career highlight is the fantastic colleagues I have had over the years who have made the work and the University a great place to be. Craig Daly Professor of Physiology, School of Cardiovasular & Metabolic Health I began as  a Trainee Technician at the University of Glasgow in July 1980, progressing  through the technical career ladder, reaching Grade 6 by the early 1990s due to  my experience working in a research lab.In 1994, I  transitioned from technical to academic roles, becoming a Research Associate  while completing a part-time PhD. After earning my PhD, I advanced to Research  Fellow, achieving Grade 8 on today’s scale, and latterly was ultimately  promoted to senior lecturer and professor. I served on the University  Court (2019-23) as a Union Rep . Having started as a trainee technician, to then be a trustee of the organisation was something that my 17-year-old self could never have imagined. Ann Hastings HR Operations Manager I have worked at the University of Glasgow all of my adult life and still love working in such a diverse environment with super bright people. Looking back, my highlights are all the jobs I have done although moving to People and Organisational Development was a revelation (in a good way!!). I love the University of Glasgow and could not imagine having worked anywhere else. 1 2 3 4 Find out from our TeamUofG what it's like to work with us View all testimonials Our inclusive community At the University of Glasgow, we believe that diversity enriches our community and drives our success as a world-leading institution. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and empowered to achieve their fullest potential. Our dedication to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion is fundamental to our academic excellence, innovation, and community engagement. We strive to eliminate barriers, challenge discrimination, and celebrate the diverse perspectives that make our community thrive. Join us as we work together to make the University of Glasgow a place where everyone belongs and can excel. Celebrate uniqueness - fostering our inclusive community Global Glasgow ​Through our strategic university partnerships, research collaborations, joint degrees, and student exchange and study abroad programmes, we are creating the opportunity for the sharing of knowledge and new ways of learning. Explore Discover our Latest Openings Test Analyst Grade 7, £41,064 - £46,049 per annum Please note this vacancy is only open to current University of Glasgow employees only. Job Purpose The Test Analyst will support high quality softw... Apply Now Assistant Demonstrator - School of Computing Science Applications for this post will only be processed where you are a University of Glasgow student and have been given the vacancy number by your Loca... Apply Now Examinations Invigilator Grade 2: £24,546 per annum pro rata This vacancy is not available to current University students.   Job Purpose   Support the smooth and secure delivery of examinations by s... Apply Now Senior Invigilator Grade 3:  £24,685 - £25,249 per annum pro rata This vacancy is not available to current University students.   Job Purpose   Support the smooth and secure delivery of examinations by s... Apply Now Organisational Development Partner Grade 8, £50,253 - £58,225 per annum Job Advert Please note that there are up to 2 positions available. These posts are full-time (35 hours per week, Monday - Friday) and open-ended (p... Apply Now Barista £13.45 p