    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/job/student-ambassador-6010576?source=google.com": {
      "title": "Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Student Ambassador · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Student Ambassador Student Ambassador Back to jobs Student Ambassador Job details Posted 28 August 2026 Salary £24,685 pa -  £25,804 pa Location Glasgow Job Type Management Professional & Administrative Reference 204733 Expiry 30 Sep 2026 23:45 Job description This role is restricted to new postgraduate taught (PGT) students joining the University of Glasgow's School of Social and Political Sciences for the 2026/27 academic year. Applicants must hold and have accepted an unconditional offer. Please confirm that you meet these criteria. Job Purpose As a Student Ambassador for the School of Social and Political Sciences, you will represent the School and University of Glasgow to prospective students from the UK and around the world. You must be a current master’s student studying on a postgraduate taught programme within the School of Social and Political Sciences. What you will do: You will support the School’s Student Recruitment and Marketing team by attending events online and in-person, speaking with prospective students, sharing your experiences and answering questions. A key aspect of this role will be leveraging your creativity, experience, and expertise to produce engaging content across multiple channels, including social media reels, TikTok videos, long-form video content, and occasional blog posts. You will create and deliver high-quality content that supports digital marketing and social media campaigns, helping to increase audience engagement and brand awareness. You should be enthusiastic about sharing your experiences of your master’s programme, student life at the University of Glasgow and living in Glasgow, helping prospective students to get a better understanding of what it is like to study here. Why become a SPS Student Ambassador? If you are passionate about your student journey and excited to help others start theirs, this is a fantastic opportunity to: Build your CV with real-world experience in communication, marketing, public engagement, and customer service capabilities. Develop valuable content creation, communication and presentation skills. Strengthen your confidence working in a professional environment. Expand your personal and professional network within the School of Social & Political Sciences and beyond. Make a meaningful impact by helping others on their postgraduate journey. Paid flexible work that can fit around your studies. How to Apply: To apply for the SPS Student Ambassador role, please submit: 1. A short video (maximum 90 seconds) explaining why you would be a great SPS Student Ambassador In your video, please tell us: *        Your name – Who are you? *        Where you're from - City and/or country *        Your Master’s degree programme *        Why you chose to study in Glasgow *        Why you would like to become an SPS Student Ambassador *        Why you're a strong fit for the role – Here you can highlight any relevant skills, experience or qualities outlined below Please send video to ssps-studentambassadors-apply@glasgow.ac.uk If shortlisted, you will be invited to a short online interview to learn a bit more about you and why you want to become a SPS Student Ambassador. If successful, we will ask you to provide a reference as part of our employment checks. However, your referee will not be contacted unless you receive an offer Main Duties and Responsibilities Sharing your experiences of being a student at the School of Social & Political Sciences to help guide others in making their decision. Engage with future students through online events, including webinars, mini lectures, and student panels, where you will share your experiences of your master’s programme and student life, participate in live Q&A sessions, and answer questions from prospective students. Attend in-person events on an occasional basis, representing the school and University and answer any questions from prospective students. You will create interesting and easy-to-understand content like videos, and social media posts and occasional blogs to show what student life is like and promote the School of Social & Political Sciences. You will participate in photo and video shoots that showcase the student experience and support the School’s promotional efforts. As this is a casual worker role, you will have the chance to choose which content tasks you want to volunteer for each month in order to earn payment. You will have to submit your timesheets each month so we can make sure you get paid on time. You will report to the Student Recruitment Lead and the Digital Marketing Lead, who will review and approve your timesheets. Maintaining clear and regular communication will be key. Knowledge, Qualifications, Skills and Experience Knowledge/Qualifications Essential: A1 Current student who is studying on a postgraduate taught (PGT) programme in the School of Social & Political Sciences A2 Enthusiastic about the University of Glasgow as a great place to study and the city of Glasgow as a great place to live Desirable: B1 Basic understanding of popular social media platforms (such as Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn) and how they are used to share information and connect with others. Skills Essential: C1 Excellent interpersonal and communication skills – friendly, professional and confident manner, comfortable with sharing your experiences as well as able to respond positively to questions and tailor your responses when needed C2 Professional approach – you will be representing the University and should always be professional C3 Excellent time-management skills and reliability – the Student Recruitment and Marketing team need to make sure that they can rely on you to attend events on time, meet deadlines that are given and engage proactively with tasks C4 Teamwork - able to work well with other ambassadors, staff, and faculty to achieve shared goals. C5 Cultural awareness - respectful and inclusive when interacting with students from many different backgrounds. C6 Initiative - willing to share ideas and take responsibility for tasks like creating content or supporting events Experience: Essential: No previous experience required; full training will be provided. Desirable: F1 Experience creating social media content for personal, academic, or community purposes. Terms and Conditions Salary will be Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum pro rata. This post is offered on a fractional basis and is fixed term until the 18th of November 2027 Closing date: 23:45 30th September 2026 As a valued member of our team, you can expect: 1 A warm welcoming and engaging organisational culture, where your talents are developed and nurtured, and success is celebrated and shared. 2 An excellent employment package with generous terms and conditions including 41 days of leave for full time staff, pension - pensions handbook https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/payandpensions/pensions/, benefits and discount packages. 3 A flexible approach to working. 4 A commitment to support your health and wellbeing, including a free 6-month UofG Sport membership for all new staff joining the University  https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/staff/healthwellbeing/. We believe that we can only reach our full potential through the talents of all. Equality, diversity and inclusion are at the heart of our values. Applications are particularly welcome from across our communities and in particular people from the Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic (BAME) community, and other protected characteristics who are under-represented within the University. Read more on how the University promotes and embeds all aspects of equality and diversity within our community https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/. We endorse the principles of Athena Swan https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/athenaswan/ and hold bronze, silver and gold awards across the University. We are investing in our organisation, and we will invest in you too. Please visit our website https://www.gla.ac.uk/explore/jobs/ for more information. Apply Now Save this job Student Ambassador Glasgow Posted 6 days ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Organisational Development Partner Glasgow Grade 8, £50,253 - £58,225 per annum Barista Glasgow £13.45 per hour Support Administrator Glasgow Grade 3, £24,685 - £25,249 per annum Clinician in Anaesthesia Glasgow Grade 7/8: £41,064 - £46,049/£50,253 - £58,225 per annum pro rata Student Ambassador Glasgow £24,685 pa -  £25,804 pa logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
